;
BYE - END YOUR CALL

CALLER. Subject to current caller access policy.

A - End your call

:A
END YOUR CALL

    BYE

Finish any transfer or message draft first. Leave the program you are
using and enter BYE at the CP/M prompt. The connection closes and the
system becomes available to the next caller.

In RBBS, C returns to CP/M and G disconnects directly. WORK is cleared
between calls; saved board messages, completed uploads and saved MESSAGE
notes remain. The mounted library disks need not return to their defaults.

BYE logs off a caller; it is not a command to shut down the host.

See HELP LOGOFF and HELP WORK.
